    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Created in 1545 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#pope-paul-iii">Pope Paul III</a> for his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#pier-luigi-farnese">Pier Luigi Farnese</a>, from territory taken from the Papal States.</li><li>Its duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#pope-paul-iii">Alessandro Farnese</a> was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#spain">Spain</a>’s leading general in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, and the Farnese were major patrons of art.</li><li>Later ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#house-of-bourbon-parma">Bourbon-Parma</a> line and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#napoleon">Napoleon</a>’s widow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#marie-louise-duchess-of-parma">Marie Louise</a>, it joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#italy">Italy</a> in 1859–1860.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The wooden <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#teatro-farnese">Teatro Farnese</a>, built in 1618 inside the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#palazzo-della-pilotta">Pilotta</a> palace, staged its first spectacle only in 1628 and was used for just a few court festivities before falling out of use.</p></aside>
    </section>

